Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Remote Preflight One-Shot Activation Ceremony P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 5d05c264-0dbe-4d8a-a5d9-e6e59c1196a4
@ [canonical_uuid] d2724a39-56bd-47ae-8787-064a6196dbfb

& [WhyNow]
  + the exact effectful runner is published but intentionally unreachable because its permit has no production constructor
  + the next useful seam is therefore not another process adapter but the authority transition that makes one invocation auditable

& [WhyCeremony]
  + a direct public constructor would collapse operator intent publication state process authority and receipt truth into one unauditable call
  + explicit stages make consent freshness scope consumption failure and final evidence separately inspectable

& [WhyAffine]
  + one non-cloneable permit consumed before runner entry prevents retries from being disguised as continuation after an uncertain physical outcome
  + terminal closure preserves honest provider-unavailable or process-refusal truth without granting repair authority

& [WhyFormationOnly]
  + operator work-slice direction authorizes repository work but does not explicitly authorize EVO-X2 contact
  + SJS can fully form and test the boundary without manufacturing the missing live decision

& [Decision]
  + form sign verify publish and bookend the provider-free ceremony contract before pure implementation
